{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>These are the living creatures that you may eat.</b> After Israel acquired their spiritual adornment at the giving of the Torah, through which they were worthy to have the Shekhinah dwell upon them without intermediary — as it says: בכל המקום אשר אזכיר את שמי אבא אליך וברכתיך (Exodus 20:21) — as will be the case in the future, as it says: ונתתי משכני בתוככם ולא תגעל נפשי אתכם (Leviticus 26:11) — the blessed El nevertheless refused to cause His Shekhinah to dwell among them any longer, as it says: כי לא אעלה בקרבך (Exodus 33:3). And Moses our Master attained through his prayer a certain rectification: that the Shekhinah would dwell among them by means of the mediation of the Tabernacle and its vessels and its ministers and its sacrifices, until they attained and merited וירא כבוד ה׳ אל כל העם (Leviticus 9:23) and the descent of fire from the heavens. Accordingly, He saw fit to rectify their temperament so that it would be prepared to shine in the light of eternal life — and this through the rectification of foods and procreation. And He prohibited the foods that defile the soul in its character traits and its intelligibles, as it says: ונטמאתם בם (Leviticus 11:43), and as it says: אל תשקצו את נפשתיכם (Leviticus 11:43), and as it says: ולא תטמאו את נפשתיכם בכל השרץ כי אני ה׳ המעלה אתכם מארץ מצרים להיות לכם לאלהים והתקדשתם והייתם קדשים (Leviticus 11:44–45) — meaning eternal, resembling the blessed Creator, as it says: כי קדוש אני (Leviticus 11:45). And He prohibited the menstruant and the zavah and the woman who gave birth, in order to sanctify the seed and purify it from all impurity, as it says: והזרתם את בני ישראל מטמאתם ולא ימתו בטמאתם בטמאם את משכני (Leviticus 15:31). And He used the language of impurity for the carcass of an unclean beast or animal, and for the eight creeping things, and for the carcass of a clean animal — for in each of these there is impurity of contact, and in some of them impurity of carrying. But those that defile the soul alone — namely fish, birds, locusts, and other creeping things that have no impurity of contact at all — He designates with the term detestable, as it says: שקץ הם לכם (Leviticus 11:10); לא יאכלו שקץ הם (Leviticus 11:13); שקץ הוא לא יאכל (Leviticus 11:41); לא תאכלום כי שקץ הם (Leviticus 11:42)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:36:13.735108367Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}